From: Vahiru <nekovahiru@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3: switch usb_0 to OTG mode with usb-role-switch

Upstream configures usb_0 (a600000.usb) with dr_mode = "host", which prevents
Android from binding the configfs USB gadget (ADB / MTP / PTP) to the port 0
DWC3 controller.

Change usb_0 to dr_mode = "otg" with usb-role-switch enabled so userspace can
switch port 0 between host and peripheral roles.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Android-specific]
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts
@@ -1287,7 +1287,9 @@
 };
 
 &usb_0_dwc3 {
-	dr_mode = "host";
+	/* Port 0 is dual-role; port 1 (a800000) hosts boot storage and stays host-only. */
+	dr_mode = "otg";
+	usb-role-switch;
 };
 
 &usb_0_dwc3_hs {
